From 2b3b314b7dce04738d813ed8e9b99dfb54aaaa15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhymabek Roman <robanokssamit@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:00:36 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.composition, frameworkudk.system, dcomp, wow64:
 Implement Windows.UI.Composition over DirectComposition

Add dlls/windows.ui.composition: the Windows.UI.Composition WinRT
runtimeclasses the Windows App SDK title-bar path activates, layered over
the DirectComposition engine. RoGetActivationFactory for
Windows.UI.Composition.Compositor resolved to nothing: the module did not
exist, combase reported the Failed-to-find-library error for the class,
the WinAppSDK title-bar object member at +0x250 stayed null, and
Window.set_ExtendsContentIntoTitleBar dereferenced it into a
System.AccessViolationException.

Compositor implements ICompositor (2.0 vtable) with CreateContainerVisual,
CreateSpriteVisual, the keyframe and expression animations, the easing
functions, InsetClip, the brushes and the batches, plus the COM interop
bridges the Windows App SDK uses: ICompositorInterop
CreateCompositionSurfaceForHandle/CreateCompositionSurfaceForSwapChain/
CreateGraphicsDevice over DCompositionCreateDevice2, and
ICompositorDesktopInterop CreateDesktopWindowTarget over
IDCompositionDesktopDevice CreateTargetForHwnd. The target answers
IDesktopWindowTargetInterop (Hwnd) for WinAppSDK. Visual, ContainerVisual,
SpriteVisual and VisualCollection carry the visual tree with parent
tracking; CompositionPropertySet stores the animated properties; every
object answers IInspectable, IAgileObject, ICompositionObject, IClosable
and its composable factory interfaces, and DllGetActivationFactory returns
E_NOINTERFACE for classes the module does not implement.

DllRegisterServer writes the ActivatableClassId registry entries; the
classes declared in classes.idl generate the registry resource.
dlls/frameworkudk.system is completed with the case-correct module name
and dlls/dcomp gains an import library. The wow64 NtAlpcSetInformation
wrapper (spec entry added by 0042) completes the syscall dispatcher.
dlls/windows.ui.composition/tests: 52 assertions over activation, the
Compositor factory QI chain, the visual tree and children, property set
round trips, brush/clip/easing construction and the desktop window target
on a real HWND; passes on x86_64.

Measured on WhatsApp Desktop 2.2620.102.0, 120 s run: the
Failed-to-find-library error for Windows.UI.Composition.Compositor
count goes 1 to 0, the Microsoft.UI.Windowing.Core.dll+0x38783
AccessViolation count goes 2 to 0, dcomp composites 48 visuals; the app
advances past title-bar construction and now stops in dxgi.dll device
creation (WIP dxgi, the next blocker).
